  "content": {
    "blocks": [
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "body": {
          "en": "HL extends SL statistics with unbiased estimators, confidence intervals, hypothesis testing, and (AI HL) the Poisson distribution.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "def",
        "label": {
          "en": "● Unbiased estimators",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "\\[\\hat{\\mu}=\\bar{x}=\\frac{\\sum x_i}{n}\\quad(\\text{unbiased for }\\mu).\\]\\[S^2=\\frac{\\sum(x_i-\\bar{x})^2}{n-1}\\quad(\\text{unbiased for }\\sigma^2;\\;\\text{use }s_{n-1}\\text{ on GDC}).\\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "thm",
        "label": {
          "en": "● Confidence interval for mean",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "\\[\\bar{x}\\pm z_{\\alpha/2}\\cdot\\frac{\\sigma}{\\sqrt{n}}\\quad(\\sigma\\text{ known}),\\qquad\\bar{x}\\pm t_{\\alpha/2,n-1}\\cdot\\frac{s}{\\sqrt{n}}\\quad(\\sigma\\text{ unknown}).\\]<p>Common critical values: 90% CI → \\(z=1.645\\); 95% CI → \\(z=1.96\\); 99% CI → \\(z=2.576.\\)</p>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "explorer",
        "title": {
          "en": "⊙ Explorer · Confidence interval for the mean",
          "ar": null
        },
        "canvasId": "ibhlCICanvas",
        "ariaLabel": {
          "en": "A normal sampling distribution for the mean, centred at x-bar with standard error s over root n, shaded to show the confidence interval",
          "ar": null
        },
        "dataPanel": {
          "btnId": "ibhlCIDataBtn",
          "panelId": "ibhlCIDataPanel",
          "descId": "ibhlCIDataDesc",
          "rowsId": "ibhlCIDataRows",
          "caption": {
            "en": "Sample statistics and the resulting interval",
            "ar": null
          },
          "columns": [
            { "en": "quantity", "ar": null },
            { "en": "value", "ar": null }
          ]
        },
        "controls": [
          {
            "id": "ibhlCIXbar",
            "label": { "en": "sample mean <b>x̄</b>:", "ar": null },
            "min": 40, "max": 60, "value": 52.3, "step": 0.1,
            "valueDisplayId": "ibhlCIXbarVal",
            "ariaLabel": { "en": "Sample mean x-bar", "ar": null }
          },
          {
            "id": "ibhlCIS",
            "label": { "en": "sample std dev <b>s</b>:", "ar": null },
            "min": 2, "max": 15, "value": 8.4, "step": 0.1,
            "valueDisplayId": "ibhlCISVal",
            "ariaLabel": { "en": "Sample standard deviation s", "ar": null }
          },
          {
            "id": "ibhlCIN",
            "label": { "en": "sample size <b>n</b>:", "ar": null },
            "min": 10, "max": 100, "value": 64, "step": 1,
            "valueDisplayId": "ibhlCINVal",
            "ariaLabel": { "en": "Sample size n", "ar": null }
          },
          {
            "id": "ibhlCILevel",
            "label": { "en": "confidence level:", "ar": null },
            "value": "95",
            "options": [
              { "value": "90", "label": "90%" },
              { "value": "95", "label": "95%", "selected": true },
              { "value": "99", "label": "99%" }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "readouts": [
          {
            "id": "ibhlCIMargin",
            "label": { "en": "margin of error", "ar": null },
            "colorClass": "amber",
            "value": "2.058"
          },
          {
            "id": "ibhlCIBounds",
            "label": { "en": "confidence interval", "ar": null },
            "colorClass": "indigo",
            "value": "(50.24, 54.36)"
          }
        ],
        "note": {
          "en": "This explorer uses the z-based formula \\(\\bar x\\pm z_{\\alpha/2}\\cdot s/\\sqrt n\\) throughout (a good approximation once \\(n\\) is reasonably large) rather than switching to the \\(t\\)-interval Worked Example 4.1 uses for its exact small-sample answer — expect the shaded interval here to be a touch narrower than that example's \\(t\\)-based one at the same 95%. The curve is the sampling distribution of the mean, width \\(s/\\sqrt n\\) — shrink it by raising \\(n\\), or widen the shaded region by demanding a higher confidence level; both change the interval for the reason the formula says they should.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "def",
        "label": {
          "en": "● Poisson distribution (AI HL)",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "\\[X\\sim\\text{Po}(\\lambda):\\quad P(X=k)=\\frac{e^{-\\lambda}\\lambda^k}{k!},\\quad\\mu=\\sigma^2=\\lambda.\\]<p>Conditions: events occur independently at a constant average rate \\(\\lambda\\) per unit interval.</p><p><strong>Poisson as approximation to Binomial:</strong> when \\(n\\) is large, \\(p\\) is small, and \\(np=\\lambda\\) is moderate.</p>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "workedExampleCard",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked Example 4.1 — CI",
          "ar": null
        },
        "problem": {
          "en": "A sample of \\(n=64\\) gives \\(\\bar{x}=52.3\\) and \\(s=8.4.\\) Construct a 95% CI for \\(\\mu.\\)",
          "ar": null
        },
        "solution": {
          "en": "<p>Use \\(t\\)-interval (\\(\\sigma\\) unknown): \\(t_{0.025,\\,63}\\approx2.00\\) (from tables or GDC).</p><p>\\(CI=52.3\\pm2.00\\cdot\\dfrac{8.4}{\\sqrt{64}}=52.3\\pm2.00(1.05)=52.3\\pm2.1=(50.2,\\;54.4).\\)</p>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "workedExampleCard",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked Example 4.2 — Poisson",
          "ar": null
        },
        "problem": {
          "en": "Cars arrive at a toll booth at a rate of 3 per minute. Find: (a) \\(P(X=5)\\); (b) \\(P(X\\ge2).\\)",
          "ar": null
        },
        "solution": {
          "en": "<p>(a) \\(P(X=5)=\\dfrac{e^{-3}\\cdot3^5}{5!}=\\dfrac{e^{-3}\\cdot243}{120}\\approx0.1008.\\)</p><p>(b) \\(P(X\\ge2)=1-P(X=0)-P(X=1)=1-e^{-3}-3e^{-3}=1-4e^{-3}\\approx1-0.1991=0.8009.\\)</p>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "explorer",
        "title": {
          "en": "⊙ Explorer · The Poisson distribution",
          "ar": null
        },
        "canvasId": "ibhlPoisCanvas",
        "ariaLabel": {
          "en": "A bar chart of the Poisson probability distribution P of X equals k, for an adjustable rate lambda",
          "ar": null
        },
        "dataPanel": {
          "btnId": "ibhlPoisDataBtn",
          "panelId": "ibhlPoisDataPanel",
          "descId": "ibhlPoisDataDesc",
          "rowsId": "ibhlPoisDataRows",
          "caption": {
            "en": "P(X = k) for every k from 0 to 15",
            "ar": null
          },
          "columns": [
            {
              "en": "k",
              "ar": null
            },
            {
              "en": "P(X = k)",
              "ar": null
            }
          ]
        },
        "controls": [
          {
            "id": "ibhlLambda",
            "label": {
              "en": "rate <b>λ</b>: ",
              "ar": null
            },
            "min": 5,
            "max": 100,
            "value": 30,
            "step": 5,
            "valueDisplayId": "ibhlLambdaLab",
            "ariaLabel": {
              "en": "Rate lambda",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "id": "ibhlPoisK",
            "label": {
              "en": "highlight <b>k</b>: ",
              "ar": null
            },
            "min": 0,
            "max": 15,
            "value": 5,
            "step": 1,
            "valueDisplayId": "ibhlPoisKlab",
            "ariaLabel": {
              "en": "k, the highlighted outcome for P(X = k)",
              "ar": null
            }
          }
        ],
        "readouts": [
          {
            "id": "ibhlMeanLam",
            "label": {
              "en": "mean μ = λ",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": "3.0",
            "colorClass": "indigo"
          },
          {
            "id": "ibhlPX5",
            "label": {
              "en": "P(X = k)",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": "0.1008",
            "colorClass": "amber"
          }
        ],
        "note": {
          "en": "Default \\(\\lambda=3\\), \\(k=5\\) is the toll-booth rate and outcome from Worked Example 4.2 — the amber bar is exactly that example's answer. Drag <b>k</b> to move the highlighted bar and read off any \\(P(X=k)\\) directly; drag \\(\\lambda\\) and watch the whole distribution's peak shift and spread out (mean = variance = \\(\\lambda\\), so a larger rate means a wider, flatter-looking bell).",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "cards",
        "items": [
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Unbiased estimator",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( s^2=\\dfrac{\\sum(x_i-\\bar{x})^2}{n-1} \\) estimates \\( \\sigma^2 \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Hypothesis test",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "State \\( H_0,H_1 \\); compute test stat; compare \\( p \\)-value to \\( \\alpha \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "warn",
        "label": {
          "en": "Practice Problem",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>A machine produces defective items at 2 per hour (Poisson). Find P(exactly 3 defective) in a 2-hour period.</p><details style=\"margin-top:8px\"><summary style=\"cursor:pointer;font-weight:600\">Show solution</summary><div style=\"margin-top:8px\"><p>\\(\\lambda=4.\\quad P(X=3)=\\frac{e^{-4}\\cdot4^3}{3!}=\\frac{64e^{-4}}{6}\\approx0.1954.\\)</p></div></details>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example-grid",
        "label": {
          "en": "Hypothesis test for population mean",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>A sample of 25 gives \\(\\bar{x}=48.2\\), \\(s=6\\). Test \\(H_0:\\mu=50\\) vs \\(H_1:\\mu\\neq50\\) at 5% significance.</p><p><strong>Solution:</strong> \\(t=\\dfrac{48.2-50}{6/\\sqrt{25}}=\\dfrac{-1.8}{1.2}=-1.5\\).</p><p>Critical value \\(t_{24,0.025}\\approx2.064\\). Since \\(|-1.5|&lt;2.064\\), do not reject \\(H_0\\).</p>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example-grid",
        "label": {
          "en": "Confidence interval",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>Construct a 95% CI for the mean of a normal population with known \\(\\sigma=8\\) given \\(n=36\\), \\(\\bar{x}=62\\).</p><p><strong>Solution:</strong> \\(\\text{CI} = \\bar{x}\\pm z_{\\alpha/2}\\cdot\\dfrac{\\sigma}{\\sqrt{n}} = 62\\pm1.96\\cdot\\dfrac{8}{6} = 62\\pm2.61 = (59.4,\\,64.6)\\)</p>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "practiceProblem",
        "question": {
          "en": "<strong>Practice:</strong> Two independent samples: \\(n_1=10,\\,\\bar{x}_1=20,\\,s_1^2=4\\) and \\(n_2=15,\\,\\bar{x}_2=18,\\,s_2^2=5\\). Test \\(H_0:\\mu_1=\\mu_2\\) at 10% using a \\(t\\)-test. State your conclusion.",
          "ar": null
        },
        "solution": {
          "en": "Pooled \\(s_p^2=\\frac{9(4)+14(5)}{23}=\\frac{106}{23}\\approx4.61\\). \\(t=\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{4.61(1/10+1/15)}}\\approx\\frac{2}{0.784}\\approx2.55\\). Critical value \\(t_{23,0.05}\\approx1.714\\). Reject \\(H_0\\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      }
    ]
  }
}
